WEBVTT

1
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.767
[Groaning]

2
00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.367
[Gasps]

3
00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.700
[Breathing heavily]

4
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:27.733
[Whimpering]

5
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:33.300
[Screams]

6
00:01:52.233 --> 00:01:53.767
[Chattering]

7
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.300
Morning. Cassie.
Glad you could join us.

8
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.767
Sorry I'm late.
Hi.

9
00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:10.600
Good morning.
Kid's late again.

10
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:13.067
Okay. you have a good day.
Mr. Rodriguez.

11
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.000
[Mr. rodriguez]
Thanks. You. too.

12
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.600
Hey. what took you so long?
I thought you left the house
right after me.

13
00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:23.133
I did.
Traffic was unbelievable.

14
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:25.800
Okay. I'll log you in.
Go get your drawer.

15
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:27.767
No. Mom. please.
I got it.

16
00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.267
Cassie. honey.
I know you want
to stay up all night

17
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.233
and talk with
your friends online.

18
00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.633
but you can't come in here
20 minutes late all the time.

19
00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.667
Mom. this is. like.
the second time
this has ever happened.

20
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.167
Just relax.

21
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.467
Actually.
it's the third.

22
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.567
If it happens
one more time.

23
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.567
Mr. crenshaw's
gonna let you go.

24
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.667
He said that?
Why doesn't he just
tell me to my face?

25
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.033
Because I'm the one
that convinced him
to hire you.

26
00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.100
That is so
passive-aggressive.

27
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.300
[Female dispatcher on radio]
Unit 6. what's your 20?

28
00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:21.800
Unit 6 at union
and west kalmia.

29
00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.667
Okay. you may not need
this job. but I do.

30
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.400
Oh. so I'm making you look bad?
Is that what you're saying?

31
00:03:27.433 --> 00:03:30.467
If I'm such an embarrassment
to you. then why do you
force me to work here?

32
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.433
Force you? Do you know
how many kids your age
are out of work?

33
00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:37.333
Besides. I thought you wanted
to save for college.

34
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:40.600
You know. lately.
I don't know about college.

35
00:03:40.633 --> 00:03:43.500
You promised me
you would enroll
at the j.C. This fall.

36
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:46.200
Maybe I changed my mind.

37
00:03:46.233 --> 00:03:49.267
[Scoffs]
When are you gonna get serious?

38
00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.467
Here we go again.
You don't want to work.

39
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.033
You don't wanna go to college
like the rest of your friends.

40
00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.133
Look. I don't care
what you do with your time.

41
00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.067
Just find something...

42
00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.067
Anything
you're passionate about...
and do it.

43
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.067
Mom. can we talk
about this at home?

44
00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.267
I'm at work.

45
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.467
Ugh! You remind me
so much of your father

46
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.333
it's not even funny.

47
00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.600
Look...

48
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:11.267
Turn around.
What... no.

49
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.167
Your hair's...
I don't need your help!

50
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.400
Your name tag's
upside down.

51
00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.067
Mom. I didn't mean it.
I just...

52
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.500
I'm sorry.

53
00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:45.333
You're right.

54
00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:48.567
It's just...
Sometimes I forget.

55
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.367
What?
That you're all grown up.

56
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.733
[Chuckles]

57
00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.633
Look. I know it's corny.

58
00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:58.100
but to me. you're...

59
00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.033
Always gonna be
my baby girl.

60
00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.167
I can help
who's next in line.

61
00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.667
[Whispers]
It's not corny.

62
00:05:17.433 --> 00:05:19.367
Oh. God. Mom...
[Man]
We're being hit!

63
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.767
[Yelling]
Don't shoot!

64
00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.567
Don't shoot!
Mom...

65
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.200
[altered voice
through speaker device]
Go!

66
00:05:25.233 --> 00:05:26.733
Move!
Yes.

67
00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:29.633
Step away
from the counters. now!
Stay down!

68
00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.467
Stay down. Stay down.
Open the door!

69
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.067
Three seconds.
and I'll shoot him!

70
00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.533
Nobody move!
[Gasps]

71
00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.733
[Voice altered
through speaker device]
Take out your cell phones. now!

72
00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.800
Toss them on the floor!
All of them!
Get down!

73
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:43.367
All the phones!
Let's go!

74
00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.100
Hurry up!
Do it!

75
00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:51.600
All right.
Everybody into the vault.
Let's go.

76
00:05:51.633 --> 00:05:54.433
Go. go. go!
Go! Get up! Go!
Okay. All right.

77
00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:56.600
Move it! Let's go!
Go. go. go. go. go!
Okay. Wait...

78
00:05:56.633 --> 00:05:59.133
Go. go! Faster!

79
00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.500
Go! Hurry up!
Ow. ow!

80
00:06:00.533 --> 00:06:03.167
Wait a minute.
You come with me.
Mom!

81
00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.433
Get in there!
Stay there!
Mom!

82
00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:08.333
[Screaming. yelling]
Get over here.

83
00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.400
Please don't hurt them.
Please. I'll do
whatever you want.

84
00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:19.667
You do everything I say.
exactly how I tell you. okay?
Okay. Yeah.

85
00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.300
Move it!

86
00:06:26.733 --> 00:06:28.767
Are you crazy?
My daughter's out there.

87
00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.767
They'll shoot you both.
I'll take my chances.

88
00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.800
Now give me that key!

89
00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:35.733
Hurry up! All of it.
Put it in the bag.

90
00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:46.667
Right on time.

91
00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:53.633
Let's go.

92
00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.700
Listen to me.
Go outside and let them in.

93
00:06:55.733 --> 00:06:57.567
Do whatever
you normally do.

94
00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.600
Don't try to give them
any kind of funny signal.

95
00:06:59.633 --> 00:07:01.433
'cause if you do.
I'll shoot you in the back.

96
00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:02.467
Go!

97
00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.733
Good morning. Cassie.

98
00:07:20.767 --> 00:07:23.167
Good morning.

99
00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.700
How's your day going?
Really good. You?

100
00:07:25.733 --> 00:07:29.167
Another day giving 100%
to the top 1%

101
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.567
so they can keep me
in the bottom 10%.

102
00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:38.133
How's your mom?
She's good.

103
00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:40.267
That woman
deserves a promotion.

104
00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.133
Five years working
for this company.

105
00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.400
and I bet she hasn't missed
a single day.

106
00:07:44.433 --> 00:07:47.400
Kind of makes you wonder
why the hell
we even do this crap.

107
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.633
Where is everybody?

108
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.333
[Grunts]

109
00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:56.367
[Whimpering]

110
00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.467
[Exhales]

111
00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.500
Bob. please.
they have my daughter.

112
00:08:06.533 --> 00:08:08.133
I cannot
just stay in here.

113
00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:10.700
What if it
was your daughter?

114
00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.667
Hurry up.
Gotta make sure.

115
00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.300
Hey. John.
you all clear?

116
00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:19.667
Hey. John. do you copy?

117
00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.633
Give me the "all clear."
buddy.

118
00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.100
Bob. please.

119
00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.667
I'm sorry. I can't.

120
00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.100
Give me that key!

121
00:08:28.133 --> 00:08:29.767
Dispatch.

122
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.133
officer's radio is 10-3.

123
00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:33.600
I'm going inside
to check it out.

124
00:08:33.633 --> 00:08:35.200
[Grunts]

125
00:08:35.233 --> 00:08:36.767
Where are you going?

126
00:08:40.533 --> 00:08:42.200
[Grunts. groans]

127
00:08:46.133 --> 00:08:47.767
Put the money
in the bag!

128
00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.067
Hurry up! Go!

129
00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.233
[Groaning continues]

130
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.733
Robbery in progress.
Shots fired.

131
00:09:13.767 --> 00:09:16.400
[Dispatcher]
Copy that. unit 6.
Police en route.

132
00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:22.333
The zipper's stuck.
What? You kidding me?

133
00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:43.333
Why are you doing this?

134
00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:48.367
Let's go.

135
00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.133
[Man]
Oh. watch out.

136
00:09:50.167 --> 00:09:52.133
[Woman]
What are you doing?
Be careful.

137
00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:54.567
Whoa. Whoa. whoa.
Watch out.

138
00:10:02.233 --> 00:10:05.300
Get in the back
of the van. quick!

139
00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:06.433
[Gunshot]

140
00:10:06.467 --> 00:10:08.200
No. don't!
Hey!

141
00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.300
What the hell
is the matter with you?

142
00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.700
[Grunting]
Stop it!

143
00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:25.133
Take it easy!

144
00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:29.367
Come on! Stop it!

145
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.600
[Sighs]

146
00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:37.533
Wait a second.
I've seen you before.

147
00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:39.767
From school.
You graduated last year.

148
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.100
She didn't graduate.
She got kicked out.

149
00:10:42.133 --> 00:10:43.633
Grace?

150
00:10:43.667 --> 00:10:46.700
Hi. Cassie.
Why is she here?

151
00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.600
She recognized me.

152
00:10:49.633 --> 00:10:51.533
Oh. that's great.
Just great.

153
00:10:51.567 --> 00:10:53.500
Are you out
of your mind?

154
00:10:53.533 --> 00:10:55.800
What the hell
is going on?

155
00:10:55.833 --> 00:10:57.467
[Grunting]

156
00:10:59.433 --> 00:11:01.733
How much you get?

157
00:11:01.767 --> 00:11:04.667
Probably twice as much
as we expected.
but so what?

158
00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.433
A hostage. abbie?
Seriously?

159
00:11:06.467 --> 00:11:09.100
I had to.
She was not
part of the plan.

160
00:11:09.133 --> 00:11:12.533
Yeah? Well. bringing live ammo
wasn't part of the plan. either.

161
00:11:12.567 --> 00:11:15.600
Wait. You did that?
Yeah. And she shot the guy
from the armored truck.

162
00:11:15.633 --> 00:11:18.133
Oh. my God.
We killed somebody.
We didn't kill him.

163
00:11:18.167 --> 00:11:19.533
He was moving when I
ran out of the truck.

164
00:11:19.567 --> 00:11:21.167
I can't believe it.
We're screwed!

165
00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.133
Everybody just chill. okay?

166
00:11:23.167 --> 00:11:25.567
We're not screwed.
It's a black market gun.

167
00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.333
I made sure to cover my ass.
unlike abbie over here.

168
00:11:28.367 --> 00:11:30.467
who stupidly decided
to bring her best friend along...

169
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.767
Her best friend
who's gonna talk.

170
00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.433
She won't.
She knows us.
She will.

171
00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.167
What were
you thinking. Joyce?

172
00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.100
You could've got us
all killed.

173
00:11:54.233 --> 00:11:56.400
[Chattering]

174
00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.633
[Police radio chatter]

175
00:12:07.533 --> 00:12:09.567
Good morning.
ladies and gentlemen.

176
00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:12.267
I am f.B.I. Agent
Christine mendoza.

177
00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.633
and I'm gonna be leading
this investigation.

178
00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:17.433
which means I'm gonna
have to speak to each
and every one of you.

179
00:12:17.467 --> 00:12:19.633
So please don't leave
the premises.

180
00:12:19.667 --> 00:12:22.333
Folks.
I'm detective barker.

181
00:12:22.367 --> 00:12:26.033
Please have a seat
in the sterile holding area
over here.

182
00:12:26.067 --> 00:12:28.333
Detective. I'm Joyce aveson.
If you need medical help...

183
00:12:28.367 --> 00:12:30.633
My daughter...
ma'am. please.
We'll be with you in a moment.

184
00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:33.300
Just take a seat.
They kidnapped my daughter.

185
00:12:33.333 --> 00:12:35.033
Come with me.

186
00:12:40.067 --> 00:12:42.567
I swear to God.
if you tell the cops I did this.

187
00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.400
I'll tell them you helped abbie
plan this whole thing.
which you practically did.

188
00:12:45.433 --> 00:12:48.500
Knock it off!
We hold Cassie until tonight.

189
00:12:48.533 --> 00:12:51.100
That'll give us time.

190
00:12:51.133 --> 00:12:54.567
You can go get out of the state.
and I can do what I gotta do.

191
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.100
[Girls grunt]

192
00:12:57.133 --> 00:12:59.033
What the hell
are you doing?

193
00:12:59.067 --> 00:13:00.667
Taking the back way.

194
00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.467
The cops will be looking for us
on the main road.

195
00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.333
[Girls grunt]

196
00:13:10.367 --> 00:13:13.500
What does she mean.
that I helped you plan this?

197
00:13:13.533 --> 00:13:16.667
Abbie. what does
she mean by that?

198
00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.100
Forget it.
The less you know. the better.

199
00:13:19.133 --> 00:13:21.100
Don't listen to Marie.
She's full of crap.
Watch your mouth.

200
00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:23.333
Wait just a minute.
So a couple weeks ago.

201
00:13:23.367 --> 00:13:26.133
when you were asking me
all those questions
about the bank...

202
00:13:26.167 --> 00:13:27.733
My schedule.

203
00:13:27.767 --> 00:13:30.133
how many employees
are there.

204
00:13:30.167 --> 00:13:33.300
the vault. what time
the armored truck arrives...

205
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.067
I thought that you
just wanted a job.

206
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.567
I was trying
to help you.

207
00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.733
And you sure as hell did.
Shut up. Marie!

208
00:13:38.767 --> 00:13:41.567
I trusted you.

209
00:13:43.467 --> 00:13:45.400
I'm sorry.

210
00:13:45.433 --> 00:13:48.467
And you set me up.

211
00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.500
How could you guys
do this to me?

212
00:13:50.533 --> 00:13:52.600
Cassie. take it easy.

213
00:13:52.633 --> 00:13:54.300
Why. abbie?
I had to!

214
00:13:56.367 --> 00:13:59.100
Grace. stop the van right now.
I'm getting out.

215
00:13:59.133 --> 00:14:01.200
Okay. cool.
So you're gonna let her
call the shots now.

216
00:14:01.233 --> 00:14:02.700
Is that what
you're gonna do. grace?

217
00:14:02.733 --> 00:14:05.033
Grace!
Cassie. calm down!

218
00:14:05.067 --> 00:14:06.567
Grace. do it now!
[Grace]
Cassie...

219
00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.667
[clamoring]

220
00:14:13.767 --> 00:14:15.233
Oh. my God!

221
00:14:15.267 --> 00:14:17.600
[Grunting. yelling]

222
00:14:23.633 --> 00:14:26.400
An armored car driver
was shot this morning

223
00:14:26.433 --> 00:14:28.700
as two heavily armed men
wearing ski masks

224
00:14:28.733 --> 00:14:30.633
held up the palm vista bank

225
00:14:30.667 --> 00:14:33.433
here on the 2300 block
of El cajon boulevard

226
00:14:33.467 --> 00:14:35.233
in downtown San Diego.

227
00:14:35.267 --> 00:14:38.200
The robbery happened
right around 9:30 A.M..

228
00:14:38.233 --> 00:14:40.433
just under an hour ago.

229
00:14:40.467 --> 00:14:43.267
Fortunately. the driver
sustained only minor bruising

230
00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.733
due to the bulletproof vest
he was wearing at the time.

231
00:14:45.767 --> 00:14:48.333
According to
the bank's manager.

232
00:14:48.367 --> 00:14:50.733
the two masked men escaped
with an undisclosed
amount of money

233
00:14:50.767 --> 00:14:54.533
and were last seen
driving away from the bank
in a green van.

234
00:14:56.767 --> 00:14:59.233
Must be nice
to work with your daughter.

235
00:14:59.267 --> 00:15:01.100
[Joyce]
It is.

236
00:15:01.133 --> 00:15:04.300
I got her the job
to spend more time with her.

237
00:15:04.333 --> 00:15:07.200
Her dad died of colon cancer
when she was ten.

238
00:15:07.233 --> 00:15:08.633
Sorry to hear that.

239
00:15:08.667 --> 00:15:11.733
I haven't really
been there for her.

240
00:15:11.767 --> 00:15:14.433
Maybe I was the reason
she was getting
into trouble at school.

241
00:15:14.467 --> 00:15:16.167
What kind of trouble?

242
00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.700
Oh. she was suspended.

243
00:15:17.733 --> 00:15:19.000
For what?

244
00:15:21.133 --> 00:15:22.433
Fighting.

245
00:15:23.567 --> 00:15:25.367
Takes after her mom.

246
00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.567
Well. I hear this morning
in the vault.

247
00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.567
you and your boss
got into it.

248
00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.633
Yeah. I was trying
to help Cassie.

249
00:15:33.667 --> 00:15:35.700
So you interrupted
an armored car driver

250
00:15:35.733 --> 00:15:37.267
who attempted
to stop the getaway?

251
00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.600
Yes. He was aiming
toward my daughter.

252
00:15:39.633 --> 00:15:41.767
I understand
how you feel.
I'm sorry.

253
00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.367
As a mother.
I believe I have the right
to protect my child.

254
00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.267
But you forget.
these armored car drivers

255
00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.767
are trained to handle
the situation.

256
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.433
Do you have children.
Ms. mendoza?

257
00:15:54.433 --> 00:15:56.533
No.

258
00:15:56.567 --> 00:16:00.200
Well. then. forgive me when
I tell you that you're wrong.

259
00:16:00.233 --> 00:16:02.133
Because there's
no possible way

260
00:16:02.167 --> 00:16:04.400
you could understand
how I feel.

261
00:16:08.333 --> 00:16:10.667
[Barker]
Mendoza.

262
00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.867
We got the surveillance video
cued up.

263
00:16:16.733 --> 00:16:18.567
Please stay put.

264
00:16:31.433 --> 00:16:33.200
[Sniffles]

265
00:17:00.567 --> 00:17:02.200
[Chuckles]

266
00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.300
Is everybody okay?

267
00:17:14.333 --> 00:17:17.200
I need help.
[Coughing]

268
00:17:21.333 --> 00:17:24.333
Easy.
I think
I messed up my leg.

269
00:17:24.367 --> 00:17:25.567
Okay.

270
00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.300
[Grunting]

271
00:17:27.333 --> 00:17:28.700
Okay.

272
00:17:28.733 --> 00:17:30.500
You okay?

273
00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.000
Cassie!

274
00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.167
[Panting]

275
00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.133
Cassie!

276
00:17:45.067 --> 00:17:46.633
Cassie. stop!

277
00:17:50.267 --> 00:17:52.333
Cassie! Cassie!

278
00:17:52.367 --> 00:17:54.667
Get off of me!
Cassie. please stop!

279
00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.667
This is how
you pay me back?
What?

280
00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.233
For last semester
in the locker room?

281
00:17:59.267 --> 00:18:01.733
I can't even believe
you're bringing that up.

282
00:18:01.767 --> 00:18:05.167
I got suspended for fighting.
for defending you.
and this is how you thank me?

283
00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.333
This is the thanks I get?

284
00:18:07.367 --> 00:18:09.200
You almost killed us.

285
00:18:09.233 --> 00:18:12.700
Marie...
I ought to pop you
right now!

286
00:18:12.733 --> 00:18:15.633
Come on. Take it easy.
I told you she'd try to run
to the cops.

287
00:18:15.667 --> 00:18:18.600
She can't afford to.
Like you said.

288
00:18:18.633 --> 00:18:21.333
if she goes to the cops.
we'll say she was in on it.

289
00:18:21.367 --> 00:18:23.133
We'll say
she's the insider.

290
00:18:23.167 --> 00:18:25.100
But that'll never happen.

291
00:18:25.133 --> 00:18:27.567
because she's gonna
do what I say.

292
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.600
Right. Cassie?

293
00:18:29.633 --> 00:18:31.667
Right.

294
00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.100
Grace and abbie...

295
00:18:34.133 --> 00:18:36.600
They might be your friends.

296
00:18:36.633 --> 00:18:38.133
Don't confuse them
with me.

297
00:18:41.567 --> 00:18:43.100
Come on.

298
00:18:48.167 --> 00:18:49.600
[Grunts]

299
00:18:49.633 --> 00:18:52.600
[Mendoza]
Okay. now check this out.

300
00:18:52.633 --> 00:18:54.433
Freeze.

301
00:18:54.467 --> 00:18:57.467
Does that look weird
to you?

302
00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.167
Yeah.

303
00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.767
Play it again.

304
00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.200
Right there.

305
00:19:04.233 --> 00:19:06.633
She says something.

306
00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:12.400
Why are you doing this?

307
00:19:12.433 --> 00:19:14.567
What do you think?

308
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.533
I think I'm gonna go talk
to the mother again.

309
00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.367
We need to pull everything
out of the van
and wipe it down.

310
00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.733
You do that.
I'm getting my money.

311
00:19:25.767 --> 00:19:28.600
I... I think
I broke my leg.

312
00:19:28.633 --> 00:19:31.300
The bone is popping out.
I am so sorry
I grabbed the wheel.

313
00:19:31.333 --> 00:19:32.567
I should never
have done that.

314
00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.200
Shut up.
Take this.

315
00:19:35.233 --> 00:19:38.000
Start picking up
the money. Go.

316
00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.800
Abbie. we gotta
get outta here.

317
00:19:40.833 --> 00:19:43.033
Yeah. No kidding.
Someone might see us.

318
00:19:43.067 --> 00:19:44.233
I got it handled.

319
00:19:44.267 --> 00:19:45.667
How?

320
00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.267
I said I got it handled.

321
00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.367
Go.

322
00:19:53.467 --> 00:19:57.367
[Barker]
A moment prior.
she's cowering in fear.

323
00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:00.100
Then.
suddenly she stands.

324
00:20:01.367 --> 00:20:03.600
and they stare
at each other

325
00:20:03.633 --> 00:20:06.300
for nearly
ten whole seconds.

326
00:20:06.333 --> 00:20:09.333
Now. I'm no psychologist.
but I'd say given the proximity.

327
00:20:09.367 --> 00:20:11.667
they seem pretty comfortable
with each other.

328
00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.433
That could mean anything.
You have no idea

329
00:20:14.467 --> 00:20:16.600
the emotional hell
she was going through
at that moment.

330
00:20:16.633 --> 00:20:19.033
Actually. I do.
Were you there?

331
00:20:19.067 --> 00:20:22.167
He was aiming a gun
at her. point-blank.

332
00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.067
Ms. aveson. I spent
ten years at the border

333
00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.700
during
the Mexican drug wars.

334
00:20:26.733 --> 00:20:29.200
El Paso. matamoros.
Tijuana.

335
00:20:29.233 --> 00:20:31.233
I've seen more
than my fair share

336
00:20:31.267 --> 00:20:34.267
of hostage situation.
kidnapping attempts
and beheadings.

337
00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:36.233
Great resume.

338
00:20:36.267 --> 00:20:37.767
You wanna impress me?

339
00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:40.200
Find my daughter.

340
00:20:40.233 --> 00:20:42.700
I think
they know each other.

341
00:20:45.667 --> 00:20:47.267
What?
[Barker]
It adds up.

342
00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.233
Body language.
the way they talk to each other.

343
00:20:50.267 --> 00:20:53.400
ten seconds
of visual recognition.

344
00:20:53.433 --> 00:20:56.433
You have got
to be kidding me.
A dozen people in a vault.

345
00:20:56.467 --> 00:20:59.433
Your daughter
is the only one chosen
to empty the cash drawers

346
00:20:59.467 --> 00:21:01.600
and escort the courier
from the armored car.

347
00:21:01.633 --> 00:21:04.633
They grabbed
the last person
to go into the vault.

348
00:21:04.667 --> 00:21:07.100
That just so happened
to be Cassie.

349
00:21:07.133 --> 00:21:09.333
You show me a video
of these bastards

350
00:21:09.367 --> 00:21:12.300
sticking a loaded gun
into my baby girl's face.

351
00:21:12.333 --> 00:21:14.733
and then you try and tell me
that she's working with them.

352
00:21:14.767 --> 00:21:16.567
Are you crazy?

353
00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:19.700
We'll talk about this later.
Please excuse us.

354
00:21:24.767 --> 00:21:27.367
[Sighs]

355
00:21:30.667 --> 00:21:34.200
[Whimpering]

356
00:21:34.233 --> 00:21:36.567
Let me check yours.
abbie.
We'll do it later.

357
00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.700
Don't worry.
You'll get your cut.

358
00:21:44.267 --> 00:21:46.400
My God. Marie!
You called your boyfriend?

359
00:21:47.833 --> 00:21:49.400
What did you tell him?

360
00:21:51.467 --> 00:21:53.667
Everything.
I kind of had to.

361
00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.633
That was not
part of the plan.

362
00:21:55.667 --> 00:21:57.733
Baby. baby!

363
00:21:57.767 --> 00:21:59.767
Nobody's supposed
to know about this!

364
00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:01.800
[Laughing]
Come here.

365
00:22:01.833 --> 00:22:03.567
[Laughing]
You all right?

366
00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:06.400
Let's see what you got.
Oh. my God.

367
00:22:06.433 --> 00:22:10.100
Oh. yeah! That's what
I'm talking about. Whoo!

368
00:22:10.133 --> 00:22:11.700
[Laughs]
Hey. Nick.

369
00:22:11.733 --> 00:22:14.233
How'd you get here
so fast?

370
00:22:14.267 --> 00:22:16.100
You live across town.

371
00:22:16.133 --> 00:22:17.267
A shortcut.

372
00:22:18.833 --> 00:22:21.733
Who's this
little sport-rocket?

373
00:22:21.767 --> 00:22:23.800
Shut up.
She's not your type.
[Chuckles]

374
00:22:23.833 --> 00:22:25.000
[Marie]
Let's go.

375
00:22:26.167 --> 00:22:28.333
Bye.
[Groaning]

376
00:22:28.367 --> 00:22:31.467
We have to get her
to a hospital now.
I know.

377
00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:34.033
Come on.
God. let's get
the hell out of here.

378
00:22:34.067 --> 00:22:36.167
Up you go.
[Nick laughing]

379
00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.667
Come on.
We gotta get somewhere.
Here.

380
00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:39.367
I got you.
Come on. come on. come on.

381
00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:41.133
[Nick laughing]

382
00:22:41.167 --> 00:22:42.633
Come on.
Yeah!

383
00:22:42.667 --> 00:22:45.133
Okay. Be careful.
[Nick]
Yeah! Whoo!

384
00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:53.133
[Chattering]

385
00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.233
[Click]

386
00:23:16.267 --> 00:23:17.233
[Printer whirrs]

387
00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:26.600
What's taking her
so long?

388
00:24:26.633 --> 00:24:28.300
[Scoffs]

389
00:24:28.333 --> 00:24:30.733
She's probably updating
her Facebook page.

390
00:24:30.767 --> 00:24:33.667
"Hey. everybody.
I just robbed a bank!

391
00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:35.533
O.M.G.! So much fun!"
[Laughs]

392
00:24:35.567 --> 00:24:37.333
You're not funny. Nick.

393
00:24:39.333 --> 00:24:41.267
So. why is it that
they brought you along?

394
00:24:41.300 --> 00:24:42.700
Your driving skills?

395
00:24:42.733 --> 00:24:45.033
Oh. kiss my ass.
Abbie needed help.

396
00:24:45.067 --> 00:24:47.400
I was the first person
she called.

397
00:24:51.333 --> 00:24:53.400
Was this worth the money?

398
00:24:53.433 --> 00:24:55.100
We didn't do it
for the money.

399
00:25:12.600 --> 00:25:13.800
Hey!

400
00:25:13.833 --> 00:25:16.400
I think they
know each other.

401
00:25:16.433 --> 00:25:17.600
[Yelling]

402
00:25:29.133 --> 00:25:30.300
Whoo!

403
00:25:30.333 --> 00:25:31.733
Wow. Nice.

404
00:25:31.767 --> 00:25:34.233
When can we take her
to the emergency room?

405
00:25:34.267 --> 00:25:36.800
Don't worry about it.
Abbie. you do what
you have to do. okay?

406
00:25:36.833 --> 00:25:39.067
[Groans]

407
00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:41.233
I promise I will get you there
as soon as I possibly can.

408
00:25:41.267 --> 00:25:42.333
Okay.

409
00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.700
That's them.

410
00:25:58.300 --> 00:26:00.300
Hello. abbie.
You got the money?

411
00:26:00.333 --> 00:26:02.300
It's right here.

412
00:26:02.333 --> 00:26:03.767
Bueno.

413
00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:05.100
Where's my dad?

414
00:26:05.133 --> 00:26:06.767
[spanish]

415
00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:08.367
[Man grunts]

416
00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:12.733
Daddy.

417
00:26:12.767 --> 00:26:14.100
I'm okay. honey.

418
00:26:14.133 --> 00:26:15.600
They hurt you.

419
00:26:15.633 --> 00:26:17.100
It looks worse than it is.

420
00:26:17.133 --> 00:26:18.667
Are you all right?

421
00:26:18.700 --> 00:26:20.367
I did what they asked.

422
00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:22.700
What?

423
00:26:22.733 --> 00:26:25.267
Oh. my God.

424
00:26:25.300 --> 00:26:27.100
Where did you get all that?
Don't worry about it.

425
00:26:27.133 --> 00:26:29.000
I'm gonna
bring you home. okay?

426
00:26:30.700 --> 00:26:33.733
Just be strong
another couple of hours.

427
00:26:33.767 --> 00:26:35.367
Abbie. what did you do?

428
00:26:37.767 --> 00:26:39.567
Dad?

429
00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:43.700
You bring $500.000
a coyote pass.

430
00:26:43.733 --> 00:26:47.233
off highway 98.
12 Miles east of ocotillo.

431
00:26:47.267 --> 00:26:50.700
You park at the road block.
then hike in half a mile.

432
00:26:50.733 --> 00:26:53.033
Okay.

433
00:26:53.067 --> 00:26:55.033
At the old water tank.
you're gonna see a road.

434
00:26:55.067 --> 00:26:57.233
Wait for us there.
Okay.

435
00:26:57.267 --> 00:26:59.767
4:00. You come alone.
No cops.

436
00:26:59.800 --> 00:27:03.500
Do exactly like I say.
or he dies.

437
00:27:03.533 --> 00:27:07.033
Oh. and I'm gonna keep
your papa's computer.
I like it.

438
00:27:07.067 --> 00:27:09.200
[Clicks off]

439
00:27:09.233 --> 00:27:11.333
[Crying]

440
00:27:20.333 --> 00:27:23.200
Hey. I just got a call
from the station.

441
00:27:23.233 --> 00:27:26.100
It looks like
they might have found
the getaway van.

442
00:27:26.133 --> 00:27:28.200
Where's the mom?

443
00:27:28.233 --> 00:27:30.200
Haven't seen her.

444
00:27:47.800 --> 00:27:50.333
[Cassie]
So how did it happen?

445
00:27:50.367 --> 00:27:54.267
You know how my dad
does real estate
in foreign countries?

446
00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:56.700
Three weeks ago.
he went down to Tijuana.

447
00:27:56.733 --> 00:27:59.633
He said they grabbed him
right off the street.

448
00:27:59.667 --> 00:28:01.733
Drug cartel. mafia...

449
00:28:01.767 --> 00:28:04.167
I have no clue who they are.

450
00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:06.100
But they called me
and told me

451
00:28:06.133 --> 00:28:08.533
that I had to give them
a half a million dollars
by today.

452
00:28:08.567 --> 00:28:11.100
or they would kill him.

453
00:28:11.133 --> 00:28:14.067
Pretty good scam.
if you ask me.
Who's asking?

454
00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:15.600
Ow. ow. ow.
Sorry.

455
00:28:15.633 --> 00:28:17.367
Why didn't you
just go to the police?

456
00:28:17.400 --> 00:28:18.667
You heard what he said.

457
00:28:18.700 --> 00:28:21.100
If I go to the cops.
they will kill him.

458
00:28:21.133 --> 00:28:24.300
Aren't they in Mexico?
I mean. how would they
even know?

459
00:28:24.333 --> 00:28:27.533
They told me that
if I tell the cops.

460
00:28:27.567 --> 00:28:31.133
the cops will tell the feds.
and the feds will tell
the Mexican government.

461
00:28:31.167 --> 00:28:33.233
and they would find out.
because they have people

462
00:28:33.267 --> 00:28:35.333
working inside
the Mexican government.

463
00:28:35.367 --> 00:28:38.100
Okay. so. why didn't you
just use your own money?

464
00:28:38.133 --> 00:28:40.233
Your father's. like.
a millionaire. right?

465
00:28:40.267 --> 00:28:42.167
This house alone
must be worth. like...
zip.

466
00:28:43.433 --> 00:28:45.167
Mortgaged to the hilt.

467
00:28:45.200 --> 00:28:48.500
My dad lost everything
in the recession.

468
00:28:48.533 --> 00:28:50.433
We have nothing.

469
00:28:50.467 --> 00:28:52.333
[Marie]
Boo-hoo.

470
00:28:52.367 --> 00:28:54.767
Poor little rich girl.
forced to live
like the rest of us.

471
00:28:57.700 --> 00:28:59.767
Ever since I lost my mom.

472
00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:02.067
it's just been me
and my dad.

473
00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:05.567
I didn't have anybody else
to turn to.

474
00:29:05.600 --> 00:29:08.300
Why didn't you
just come to me

475
00:29:08.333 --> 00:29:10.733
instead of doing all this
behind my back?

476
00:29:10.767 --> 00:29:14.267
If I had.
would you have helped me
rob the bank?

477
00:29:16.333 --> 00:29:19.333
That is 370.000
United States currency. baby.

478
00:29:19.367 --> 00:29:21.200
and that's just
what's in this bag.

479
00:29:21.233 --> 00:29:24.067
Whoo! Give me the bag
so I can check the rest of it.

480
00:29:27.667 --> 00:29:29.567
Let go. Marie.
No. you let go.

481
00:29:31.167 --> 00:29:32.767
[Grunts]

482
00:29:32.800 --> 00:29:34.467
What was that?

483
00:29:38.833 --> 00:29:40.600
Someone pulled
in front of your house.

484
00:29:44.667 --> 00:29:46.667
It's Cassie's mom.

485
00:29:46.700 --> 00:29:49.100
Mom...
Grace...

486
00:29:49.133 --> 00:29:51.867
[muffled shouts]
She saw me!

487
00:29:55.733 --> 00:29:57.700
Hurry up!
Put Cassie in the bedroom!

488
00:29:57.733 --> 00:30:00.100
Nick. get the money
off the table!

489
00:30:00.133 --> 00:30:02.700
You kidding me? I just
finished stacking this up.
Nick. now!

490
00:30:02.733 --> 00:30:04.467
No. I don't think so.
Bring me the other bag.

491
00:30:04.500 --> 00:30:06.033
I'll count it.
Abbie!

492
00:30:06.067 --> 00:30:08.200
Hurry up! Go! Now!
Freaking kidding me.

493
00:30:10.567 --> 00:30:12.700
Come on. come on. come on!

494
00:30:18.167 --> 00:30:19.200
[Joyce]
Abbie!

495
00:30:21.267 --> 00:30:23.333
I know you're in there!

496
00:30:23.367 --> 00:30:24.767
[Groaning]
Easy.

497
00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:26.433
Please open this door.

498
00:30:26.467 --> 00:30:29.200
If you say a word
you're dead.

499
00:30:29.233 --> 00:30:32.367
If your mom walks
through that door right now.
I'm gonna shoot her in the face.

500
00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:34.333
[Joyce]
Abbie!

501
00:30:34.367 --> 00:30:37.133
Ow!

502
00:30:37.167 --> 00:30:39.300
Here. Right there.

503
00:30:39.333 --> 00:30:41.367
Abbie. I need to talk
to you now. please.

504
00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:43.567
You know that I saw you.
Please open this door.

505
00:30:43.600 --> 00:30:46.067
What are you doing?

506
00:30:46.100 --> 00:30:48.400
Abbie!

507
00:30:48.433 --> 00:30:51.533
Everybody be really quiet.

508
00:30:56.833 --> 00:30:59.600
Hi. Joyce.
Good morning.

509
00:30:59.633 --> 00:31:03.100
Hi. Abbie. I don't suppose
your dad's home?

510
00:31:03.133 --> 00:31:07.467
Mm-mm. He's on
a business trip. Why?

511
00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:09.233
Where's Cassie?

512
00:31:09.267 --> 00:31:12.067
W... um. she's not here.

513
00:31:12.100 --> 00:31:13.400
Abbie. don't lie to me.

514
00:31:13.433 --> 00:31:15.533
I'm not lying.

515
00:31:15.567 --> 00:31:18.367
Is Cassie in some kind
of trouble or something?

516
00:31:18.400 --> 00:31:20.800
I don't know.
Is she?

517
00:31:20.833 --> 00:31:24.133
You're really starting
to scare me.
What is going on?

518
00:31:24.167 --> 00:31:26.433
I think you know
exactly what's going on.

519
00:31:26.467 --> 00:31:28.400
I do? Because I...
Cassie!

520
00:31:28.433 --> 00:31:30.600
What... hang on!
Cassie!

521
00:31:30.633 --> 00:31:34.033
Wait... no.
She's with you. right?
She's working today.

522
00:31:34.067 --> 00:31:36.133
Stop with the act.
I know you were
at the bank today.

523
00:31:36.167 --> 00:31:37.667
Where is she?

524
00:31:37.700 --> 00:31:40.100
At the bank.
She's not at the bank.

525
00:31:40.133 --> 00:31:42.667
You took Cassie hostage.
What?

526
00:31:42.700 --> 00:31:45.233
I could've told the police.
I didn't.

527
00:31:45.267 --> 00:31:47.033
All I want is my daughter.

528
00:31:47.067 --> 00:31:49.733
Please. Where is she?
Joyce. slow down.

529
00:31:49.767 --> 00:31:52.700
[Whispering]
I saw a big roll of plastic
in the garage.

530
00:31:52.733 --> 00:31:55.433
We dig a hole in the desert.
get rid of both of them.

531
00:31:55.467 --> 00:31:57.233
[Whispering]
Shut up.

532
00:31:57.267 --> 00:32:00.067
[No audible dialogue]

533
00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:02.333
What is that?

534
00:32:02.367 --> 00:32:04.700
This is a still frame

535
00:32:04.733 --> 00:32:07.067
from security video
at the bank.

536
00:32:07.100 --> 00:32:10.533
This is the wrist
of the person who robbed us
this morning.

537
00:32:10.567 --> 00:32:13.333
My God. are you okay?
Was anybody hurt?

538
00:32:13.367 --> 00:32:15.533
Abbie. stop it.

539
00:32:15.567 --> 00:32:18.100
I was with Cassie
when she bought that for you.

540
00:32:19.833 --> 00:32:22.300
A million people
have bracelets like that.

541
00:32:22.333 --> 00:32:24.733
Cut the bull!

542
00:32:24.767 --> 00:32:28.767
No offense.
but are you on. like.

543
00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:32.367
some kind of medication
or something?

544
00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:34.800
Because none of this
makes any sense.

545
00:32:34.833 --> 00:32:37.033
A few weeks ago.
Cassie told me
you were asking her

546
00:32:37.067 --> 00:32:38.533
a lot of questions
about her job.

547
00:32:38.567 --> 00:32:39.767
Yeah?

548
00:32:39.800 --> 00:32:42.533
Why were you so curious?

549
00:32:42.567 --> 00:32:45.467
Joyce. be real.

550
00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:49.233
Do you really think
that I'm the kind of girl
who would rob a bank?

551
00:32:49.267 --> 00:32:52.567
You're telling me
that you have been here
all morning. alone?

552
00:32:52.600 --> 00:32:54.700
Yeah.

553
00:32:54.733 --> 00:32:57.233
Prove it.

554
00:32:57.267 --> 00:33:01.133
I guess you're just gonna
have to take my word for it.

555
00:33:01.167 --> 00:33:03.233
No. I'm gonna look
in every room in this house.

556
00:33:03.267 --> 00:33:05.467
I'm gonna go out there
and shoot her right now.
Wait. wait.

557
00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:09.600
Cassie?
Get in the bathroom.
Get in the bathroom.

558
00:33:09.633 --> 00:33:12.333
Cassie. are you back here?
Wait! Joyce. wait!

559
00:33:12.367 --> 00:33:14.267
Ms. aveson. please!

560
00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:16.800
Cassie.
are you back here?
Wait!

561
00:33:16.833 --> 00:33:18.233
Oh. Hey.

562
00:33:19.600 --> 00:33:21.267
Baby. what's going on?

563
00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:23.167
Um...

564
00:33:26.367 --> 00:33:29.433
This is. um...

565
00:33:29.467 --> 00:33:32.367
This is my friend's mom.

566
00:33:32.400 --> 00:33:34.067
Oh. hi. I'm Jack.

567
00:33:34.100 --> 00:33:36.100
[Nick. abbie chuckle]

568
00:33:36.133 --> 00:33:38.167
Babe. why don't you
go back to bed?

569
00:33:38.200 --> 00:33:40.167
I'll be in
in a minute.

570
00:33:40.200 --> 00:33:41.367
Are you sure?
Yes.

571
00:33:43.667 --> 00:33:45.200
Mm.

572
00:33:50.667 --> 00:33:52.700
[Sighs]
I love you.

573
00:33:52.733 --> 00:33:55.100
I love you. too.
[Chuckles]

574
00:33:55.133 --> 00:33:57.067
I can't get
enough of this.

575
00:33:57.100 --> 00:33:58.567
[Laughs]

576
00:33:58.600 --> 00:34:00.533
[Nick. abbie chuckle]

577
00:34:07.233 --> 00:34:08.733
I'm sorry I lied.

578
00:34:08.767 --> 00:34:11.200
I wasn't alone.

579
00:34:11.233 --> 00:34:13.367
Please don't
tell my dad.

580
00:34:13.567 --> 00:34:16.567
I guess I owe you
an apology.

581
00:34:16.600 --> 00:34:19.433
I'm sorry.

582
00:34:19.467 --> 00:34:23.000
It's okay.
You've been through
a lot this morning.

583
00:34:24.467 --> 00:34:26.767
What about Cassie?

584
00:34:26.800 --> 00:34:29.267
Do the police have any idea
where they took her?

585
00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:31.733
No. not yet. Um...

586
00:34:31.767 --> 00:34:34.400
The cops said that

587
00:34:34.433 --> 00:34:36.567
once the bank robbers
get far enough away.

588
00:34:36.600 --> 00:34:39.033
they usually
let the hostage go.

589
00:34:39.067 --> 00:34:41.033
But I guess I'll just
have to wait and see.

590
00:34:41.067 --> 00:34:43.100
I'm really sorry.

591
00:34:46.133 --> 00:34:50.767
What's this...
Coyote pass off highway 98?

592
00:34:50.800 --> 00:34:53.167
Oh. that's just
a message for my dad.

593
00:34:53.200 --> 00:34:57.133
Some guy called about
some kind of development
out in the desert.

594
00:34:57.167 --> 00:35:00.167
I'll have to remember
to give that to him.

595
00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:02.533
I'll let myself out.

596
00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:08.733
[Wincing]

597
00:35:40.100 --> 00:35:41.700
[Sighs]
She's gone!

598
00:35:41.733 --> 00:35:43.233
[Mutters]
[Grunts]

599
00:35:45.533 --> 00:35:46.700
Go!

600
00:35:55.700 --> 00:35:57.400
Hey. that's twice today
I've saved your bacon.

601
00:35:57.433 --> 00:36:00.433
Least you could do
is say "thank you."

602
00:36:00.467 --> 00:36:04.600
I'm not sensing
gratitude right now.
No.

603
00:36:04.633 --> 00:36:07.200
I think abbie
needs to learn
that it's better to give

604
00:36:07.233 --> 00:36:10.267
than receive.

605
00:36:10.300 --> 00:36:12.133
[Cassie]
Abbie...

606
00:36:12.167 --> 00:36:14.400
We're taking it all.

607
00:36:14.433 --> 00:36:16.700
We had a deal.
I changed the deal.

608
00:36:16.733 --> 00:36:20.067
Marie. please.
Between your bag and mine.

609
00:36:20.100 --> 00:36:22.200
I'm sure we've got over
a million dollars right now.

610
00:36:22.233 --> 00:36:25.133
Our agreement was to keep
everything over 500.000.

611
00:36:26.333 --> 00:36:28.167
That's not enough for you?

612
00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:30.233
I've expensive taste.

613
00:36:30.267 --> 00:36:32.733
Okay. what about abbie's dad?
You saw what they did to him.

614
00:36:32.767 --> 00:36:35.200
If they don't get
the money they asked for.
they're gonna kill him.

615
00:36:35.233 --> 00:36:37.267
That's abbie's problem.
not mine.

616
00:36:38.700 --> 00:36:40.367
Let's go.

617
00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:43.033
I say we kill all three of them.
cover our tracks.

618
00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:46.400
It's not required.
What if they talk?

619
00:36:46.433 --> 00:36:49.600
Then they'll get 30 to life
for armed robbery.

620
00:36:49.633 --> 00:36:52.400
They're stupid.
but they're not that stupid.

621
00:36:52.433 --> 00:36:53.700
Come on.
Let's hit it.

622
00:36:57.467 --> 00:36:59.133
Marie.

623
00:37:05.333 --> 00:37:07.400
Come on.

624
00:37:09.400 --> 00:37:11.267
You think you're better
than me. don't you?

625
00:37:16.667 --> 00:37:18.533
Come on.

626
00:37:39.300 --> 00:37:42.033
What's happening?
We need to get outta here
right now.

627
00:37:42.067 --> 00:37:45.433
Why?
Because Nick and Marie
are gonna be back any second.

628
00:37:45.467 --> 00:37:47.667
and this time.
they will kill us.

629
00:37:47.700 --> 00:37:49.467
Move.
But...

630
00:37:51.433 --> 00:37:54.433
Mm.
[Sighs]

631
00:37:54.467 --> 00:37:56.533
When we get
to the hotel in Reno.

632
00:37:56.567 --> 00:37:58.533
I'm gonna throw this money
all over the bed.

633
00:37:58.567 --> 00:38:00.133
Oh. yeah?
Mm-hmm.

634
00:38:00.167 --> 00:38:02.300
And then I'm gonna
throw you on top of it...

635
00:38:02.333 --> 00:38:04.333
[Chuckles]
And then I'm gonna
take off my...

636
00:38:07.767 --> 00:38:09.133
What the hell is this?

637
00:38:11.533 --> 00:38:13.567
[Yells]
You gotta be kidding me.

638
00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:15.500
[Marie screaming]

639
00:38:15.533 --> 00:38:18.367
I'm gonna kill her!
I'm gonna kill her!

640
00:38:18.400 --> 00:38:19.667
[Screams]

641
00:38:26.733 --> 00:38:31.300
Cassie. I'm gonna drop you off
a couple blocks away
from the hospital.

642
00:38:31.333 --> 00:38:34.433
I know that I have no right
to ask you for a favor.

643
00:38:34.467 --> 00:38:37.167
but can you please wait

644
00:38:37.200 --> 00:38:39.767
to talk to the cops
until after 4:00?

645
00:38:39.800 --> 00:38:41.733
Just give me that time
to get my dad back.

646
00:38:41.767 --> 00:38:44.600
Can you promise me that?
Yes. Yeah.
I'm just worried about...

647
00:38:44.633 --> 00:38:47.133
Abbie. let's go.
Okay.

648
00:38:47.167 --> 00:38:50.167
We're gonna take my dad's car
so grace can fit
in the back seat.

649
00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:52.067
[Grunts]

650
00:38:54.500 --> 00:38:55.633
[Yells]

651
00:39:00.300 --> 00:39:01.633
Okay.

652
00:39:30.433 --> 00:39:31.267
Hold on.
hold on. hold on.
Damn it!

653
00:39:31.300 --> 00:39:34.400
The car is gone!

654
00:39:49.467 --> 00:39:51.400
Check upstairs.
Yeah.

655
00:40:03.300 --> 00:40:05.267
They're not here.

656
00:40:11.067 --> 00:40:13.300
[Yells]

657
00:40:13.333 --> 00:40:16.333
[Police radio chatter]

658
00:40:16.367 --> 00:40:19.467
[Mendoza]
So what exactly did you see?

659
00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:22.033
Well.
there were four women

660
00:40:22.067 --> 00:40:24.233
who came from the van.

661
00:40:24.267 --> 00:40:26.667
and then they walked
up that hill. and...

662
00:40:26.700 --> 00:40:30.133
A brown truck arrived.
and a man stepped out.

663
00:40:30.167 --> 00:40:32.667
and then everyone got in.
They drove off.

664
00:40:32.700 --> 00:40:36.133
Women? You're sure?

665
00:40:36.167 --> 00:40:40.567
Yes. I'm pretty sure I know
what a woman looks like. dear.

666
00:40:40.600 --> 00:40:43.067
What age were they?

667
00:40:43.100 --> 00:40:47.200
Well. the guy
was in his late 20's.

668
00:40:47.233 --> 00:40:50.400
and the girls
were college age.

669
00:40:50.433 --> 00:40:51.500
High school. maybe.

670
00:40:51.533 --> 00:40:54.100
And what ethnicity
were they?

671
00:40:54.133 --> 00:40:56.233
Well. they were all white.

672
00:40:56.267 --> 00:40:58.567
except one girl
was African-American.

673
00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:02.333
Looks like
she'd broken a leg.
They were helping her walk.

674
00:41:02.367 --> 00:41:04.567
This is a long shot.

675
00:41:04.600 --> 00:41:06.667
but any of the girls
look like this?

676
00:41:06.700 --> 00:41:09.300
You know. I was standing
all the way over there.

677
00:41:09.333 --> 00:41:11.433
I'm not sure...

678
00:41:11.467 --> 00:41:14.700
Yes. Possibly.

679
00:41:14.733 --> 00:41:17.067
Yes. one girl
did look like her.

680
00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:19.433
Okay.
Thank you. Mrs. Wells.

681
00:41:19.467 --> 00:41:22.067
Agent mendoza.
before you leave.

682
00:41:22.100 --> 00:41:24.133
maybe you could help me.

683
00:41:24.167 --> 00:41:26.467
I'm looking
for someone.

684
00:41:26.500 --> 00:41:29.133
His name is Gary.
Gary Wells.

685
00:41:29.167 --> 00:41:31.767
He's seven years old.

686
00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:35.467
He should be back by now.
but I haven't seen him yet.

687
00:41:35.500 --> 00:41:39.133
I'm very. very worried.
and I want you
to look for him. please.

688
00:41:39.167 --> 00:41:40.433
Okay. I'll do that.

689
00:41:44.767 --> 00:41:46.033
I'll wait for your call.

690
00:41:50.167 --> 00:41:52.700
All right.
I want you to alert every
emergency room in the area

691
00:41:52.733 --> 00:41:54.700
to be on the lookout
for an African-American girl.

692
00:41:54.733 --> 00:41:57.567
18 to 25.
with a sprained ankle
or a broken leg.

693
00:41:57.600 --> 00:41:59.767
Whoa. Wait a minute.
You don't actually believe
what she said?

694
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:02.133
My grandfather
was the same way.

695
00:42:02.167 --> 00:42:03.700
One second. he'd be sharp.

696
00:42:03.733 --> 00:42:05.800
The next second.
he'd be...

697
00:42:05.833 --> 00:42:07.700
Floating off
to another planet.

698
00:42:09.200 --> 00:42:11.133
Not gonna
hold up in court.

699
00:42:18.767 --> 00:42:20.767
[Cassie]
How did you know
they would rob you?

700
00:42:20.800 --> 00:42:23.600
I didn't.
But when we flipped the van.

701
00:42:23.633 --> 00:42:26.633
Nick came to pick us up
way too fast.

702
00:42:26.667 --> 00:42:30.400
And then when we got home.
I saw footprints in the house.

703
00:42:30.433 --> 00:42:32.433
and the back door
was unlocked.

704
00:42:32.467 --> 00:42:34.367
I always lock that door.

705
00:42:34.400 --> 00:42:36.133
My guess is.

706
00:42:36.167 --> 00:42:38.400
while we
were robbing the bank.

707
00:42:38.433 --> 00:42:40.733
Nick broke into the house

708
00:42:40.767 --> 00:42:44.167
and was waiting
to ambush us when we got there.

709
00:42:44.200 --> 00:42:46.200
But then Marie called him
to come pick us up.
Yeah?

710
00:42:46.233 --> 00:42:48.100
Come get us.
We crashed the van.
You what?

711
00:42:48.133 --> 00:42:49.700
You heard me!
You got the money. right?

712
00:42:49.733 --> 00:42:51.467
Shut up. and get over
to the old dirt road!

713
00:42:51.500 --> 00:42:53.700
Yeah. I'll be right there.
Regardless.

714
00:42:53.733 --> 00:42:56.133
he and Marie were planning
to screw me over all along.

715
00:42:56.167 --> 00:42:59.400
So while you guys were waiting
outside in the car.

716
00:42:59.433 --> 00:43:03.500
I counted the cash.
and I put it underneath
the bathroom sink

717
00:43:03.533 --> 00:43:07.233
and replaced it with
my dad's paperback collection.

718
00:43:12.800 --> 00:43:15.067
Hello. This is Joyce.

719
00:43:15.100 --> 00:43:17.767
Mrs. aveson.
this is detective mendoza.

720
00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:20.233
I've got some new evidence
involving your daughter.

721
00:43:21.367 --> 00:43:23.133
What is it?

722
00:43:23.167 --> 00:43:25.667
I'd like to discuss it
in person.

723
00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:28.733
Can you meet me at
the f.B.I. Headquarters
on 3rd street?

724
00:43:45.400 --> 00:43:47.400
One last favor:

725
00:43:47.433 --> 00:43:50.500
When you talk to the police.
leave grace's name out of it.

726
00:43:50.533 --> 00:43:52.600
Um. hello! Thank you.

727
00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:57.367
Cassie.
I don't have that long.

728
00:43:57.400 --> 00:43:59.133
Are you really gonna
go talk to the kidnappers
without any protection at all.

729
00:43:59.167 --> 00:44:01.133
like a gun or anything?
Do I have a choice?

730
00:44:01.167 --> 00:44:04.567
I mean.
my life's over.

731
00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:07.100
I'm gonna go to jail
either way.

732
00:44:07.133 --> 00:44:09.033
But I'm gonna try to get
my dad back first.

733
00:44:11.300 --> 00:44:14.033
I'll see you later.

734
00:44:14.067 --> 00:44:15.700
Okay.

735
00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:32.267
I'm coming with you.

736
00:44:32.300 --> 00:44:33.567
[Grunts]

737
00:44:33.600 --> 00:44:36.200
Cassie...
Just shut up and drive.

738
00:44:44.667 --> 00:44:46.800
[Joyce]
So when do you think
this happened?

739
00:44:46.833 --> 00:44:50.500
According to eyewitnesses.
the car crashed
at about 10:30 A.M..

740
00:44:50.533 --> 00:44:52.367
45 minutes
after the robbery.

741
00:44:52.400 --> 00:44:56.067
But by the time we got there.
the car was already abandoned.

742
00:44:56.100 --> 00:44:58.667
Do you know if Cassie
was with them?

743
00:44:58.700 --> 00:45:02.033
Somebody who looks
like your daughter
was seen there.

744
00:45:02.067 --> 00:45:04.233
along with a man
in his late 20's

745
00:45:04.267 --> 00:45:06.600
and three girls
approximately Cassie's age.

746
00:45:06.633 --> 00:45:09.100
one of whom
had a broken leg.

747
00:45:09.133 --> 00:45:13.367
Ms. aveson. three teenage girls
robbed your bank this morning.

748
00:45:16.600 --> 00:45:18.700
The reason I called you
in here today

749
00:45:18.733 --> 00:45:21.333
is 'cause I need to talk to you
about Cassie's friends.

750
00:45:21.367 --> 00:45:24.333
I'm gonna need a list from you
of names. e-mail addresses...

751
00:45:24.367 --> 00:45:27.533
No. Cassie's friends
are all going to college.

752
00:45:27.567 --> 00:45:29.800
Trust me. they're not
spending their summer break
robbing banks.

753
00:45:29.833 --> 00:45:32.700
